Children and Social Welfare</publisher-name></citation></ref><ref id="B13"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Osrin</surname><given-names>D</given-names></name><name><surname>Tumbahangphe</surname><given-names>KM</given-names></name><name><surname>Shrestha</surname><given-names>D</given-names></name><name><surname>Mesko</surname><given-names>N</given-names></name><name><surname>Shrestha</surname><given-names>BP</given-names></name><name><surname>Manandhar</surname><given-names>MK</given-names></name><name><surname>Standing</surname><given-names>H</given-names></name><name><surname>Manandhar</surname><given-names>DS</given-names></name><name><surname>Costello</surname><given-names>AM de L</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Cross sectional, community based study of care of newborn infants in Nepal.</article-title><source>Br Med J</source><year>2002</year><volume>325</volume><fpage>1063</fpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">12424164</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1136/bmj.325.7372.1063</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B14"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Tamang</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name><name><surname>Mesko</surname><given-names>N</given-names></name><name><surname>Shrestha</surname><given-names>BP</given-names></name><name><surname>Osrin</surname><given-names>D</given-names></name><name><surname>Manandhar</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><name><surname>Standing</surname><given-names>H</given-names></name><name><surname>Manandhar</surname><given-names>DS</given-names></name><name><surname>Shrestha</surname><given-names>JR</given-names></name><name><surname>Costello</surname><given-names>AM</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>A qualitative description of perinatal care practices in Makwanpur district, Nepal</article-title><source>Contributions to Nepalese Studies</source><year>2001</year><volume>28<